      "writtenOn": "2020-06-08T23:27:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is what I had originally. \n\nWe had a long discussion about this on the older patchsets, there are situations where we will need to configure both the PPC and TCPC to enable FRS (ex. Zork) So, the CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_PPC/TCPC is used to designate where the FRS trigger is. Since we may still need to configure both the TCPC and PPC depending on which TCPC/PPC we\u0027re using though, I moved these checks to the TCPC/PPC driver itself.\n\nIs there a better way to handle these situations? We could have both CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_TCPC and PPC co-exist, but then there could be ambiguity to where the trigger is implemented (ex PS8815 + syv682).",
      "parentUuid": "309b5911_b131fd6a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 734,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 734,
        "endChar": 34
